  "final_answer": "Based on my exploration of the knowledge graph, I found three studio members connected to the Beacon Grid project through \"mentions\" edges. However, the graph structure alone doesn't contain role information—that would be in the actual record content, which the available tools cannot read.\n\n**Studio members connected to Beacon Grid:**\n\n1. **Noor Haddad** — linked to `projects/beacon-grid.md` (also connected to Ledgerline and Wayfare projects)\n2. **Silas Brandt** — linked to `projects/beacon-grid.md` (also connected to Larkspur Archive project)\n3. **Theo Kanda** — linked to `projects/beacon-grid.md` (also connected to Kestrel CRM and Meridian Studio org)\n\n**Evidence:**\n- `projects/beacon-grid.md` has incoming \"mentions\" edges from `people/noor-haddad.md`, `people/silas-brandt.md`, and `people/theo-kanda.md`\n- Paths from `orgs/meridian-studio.md` to `projects/beacon-grid.md` traverse through Theo Kanda and Noor Haddad\n\n**Limitation:** The graph tools (lookup, neighbors, paths) only reveal typed edges between records, not the markdown content within them. Specific roles (e.g., \"lead engineer,\" \"designer,\" \"PM\") would be documented inside the people or project records themselves, which I cannot access with the current toolset.\n\nIf you have access to the actual markdown files, checking `people/noor-haddad.md`, `people/silas-brandt.md`, `people/theo-kanda.md`, and `projects/beacon-grid.md` directly would reveal the role details.",
